:"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":18214,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1927,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/68917","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/68917","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/68917.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/68917.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-13T19:53:22Z"},"body":"A single broken deadline alert could stop a Dag run from being created. Deadline alerts are evaluated while the run is being created, and any failure there (a corrupt stored alert, an interval Variable that is missing or not a number, a reference that fails to evaluate) raised straight through and took the run down with it. If a Dag had several alerts, the first failure also starved the rest of their deadlines.\n\nThis change makes deadline alert creation best effort: a failing alert is logged and skipped, the run is still created, and the remaining alerts still get their deadlines. Skips are counted in a new `deadline_alerts.deadline_creation_failed` metric, tagged the same way as the existing `deadline_created` one, so they are visible rather than silent.\n\nOne small change rides along: an absurdly large interval value now surfaces as the same validation error as a non-numeric one, instead of escaping as a low-level overflow error.\n\nScope note: this PR previously also carried the VariableInterval resolution mechanics. Those have landed or moved elsewhere and are no longer part of this change. #71802 (merged) introduced the serialized interval type and dispatch; #71968 (open) covers resolving the interval on the caller's database session. What remains here is only the failure isolation.\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes (please specify the tool below)\n\nGenerated-by: Claude Code (Fable 5) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/68917/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/68917/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":29646019443,"node_id":"LE_lADOAgUK288AAAABNSHkT88AAAAG5wpbcw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/29646019443","actor":{"login":"dosubot[bot]","id":131922026,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOB9z4ag","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/324583?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dosubot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dosubot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dosubot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dosubot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dosubot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dosubot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptio